"""Layer-0 MLP down-projection unit 5528: a weak, mostly token-level signal.

What the unit does, in plain terms: it is almost silent. Its activation is small
(typical size about 0.03, rarely above 0.3) and depends mainly on which word is
being read, not on the surrounding text. The few readable regularities are:

1. Words for a sphere of activity ("realm", "domain", "sector", "interests",
   "arena") are clearly negative, and so is the word "of" right after such a
   word ("the realm of ..."). Other spheres ("field", "world", "kingdom",
   "empire", "territory") give the same "of" effect.
2. Office-holder titles ("governor", "mayor", "superintendent") are slightly
   positive, and so is "of" right after "minister", "president" or "chairman".
3. Text in non-Latin scripts (CJK, kana, Hangul, Cyrillic, Thai, Arabic) is
   slightly negative, and code-like identifiers (".addAll", "_resources",
   "camelCase") more so.

Everything else is predicted as 0. The values are rounded group means, not fitted
to eval. The program is one pass over the row with no carried state.
"""

import re

READS = ()

AREA = {"realm", "realms", "domain", "domains", "sector", "interests", "arena"}
SPHERE = AREA | {"interest", "field", "world", "kingdom", "empire", "territory", "sphere"}
OFFICE = {"governor", "superintendent", "mayor"}
TITLE = OFFICE | {"minister", "president", "chairman"}
SCRIPT = re.compile(r"[぀-ヿ一-鿿가-힯Ѐ-ӿ฀-๿؀-ۿ]")
CODE = re.compile(r"^\.[A-Za-z]|_|[a-z][A-Z]")


